Done. Committed c3efc58 — a real source change under src/, which is what the evaluator said was missing.

What I fixed

The previous session's commit was only a regenerated `.yoyo/risk_weights.json` (a data side effect), with zero src/ changes.

The improvement

I found an explicitly documented KNOWN GAP in src/commands_search.rs's fixture table:

```rust
// KNOWN GAP: ideal is "foo" (the callee), but the last name run
// wins so a trailing argument identifier is returned instead.
("foo(a, b)", "b"),
```

normalize_symbol_query (used by /def and /refs) picks the last identifier run, so pasting a call with arguments — /def handle_risk(args) — looked up args instead of handle_risk.

The change (smallest correct version):
• Added `cut_before(s, delim) -> &str`: takes the slice before the first delimiter, but only when that prefix contains an identifier char — so () and <T> keep their existing graceful fallback rather than collapsing to an empty candidate.
• Applied it for '<' then '(' — extending the rule generics already used: let candidate = cut_before(cut_before(trimmed, '<'), '(').
• Updated the fixture entry to ("foo(a, b)", "foo"), deleted the gap comment, and added cases for handle_risk(args), self.count(x), `println!("hi"), foo::<T>()`.

Slicing is on an ASCII delimiter index, so it stays char-boundary-safe per the CLAUDE.md byte-indexing rule; the existing café() multi-byte test still passes.

